# Tests excluded from `cargo miri test`. Each entry must carry a
# one-line justification. Format: `<module-path>::<test-name>  # reason`
# Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored.
#
# Categories Miri cannot model and which therefore must be skipped:
#   - real filesystem semantics (metadata, mtime, symlinks, mmap)
#   - foreign-function calls into libc beyond the modelled core surface
#   - cargo-llvm-cov instrumentation (Miri runs unoptimised, no llvm-tools)
#
# Allow-list intent: stay under 20 entries. Each entry should be
# revisited when Miri ships new model coverage.

# Filesystem semantics — Miri's shim does not implement create_dir_all
# atomically and the dirstamp-driven cache test reads st_mtime from the
# host kernel, which Miri's emulation reports as constant.
core::cache::tests::dirstamp_changes_invalidate_cache
plugin::cache::persists_across_runs

# fail-rs failpoint registration uses TLS in a way Miri can't model
# under -Zmiri-track-stacked-borrows; we exercise these paths in the
# native test job (`test` matrix in ci.yml).
fault_injection_failpoint_smoke
